tic because he wouldn't  make them about an older man for example  but let's first check out the ever so  controversial video of her partying and  having a good time  [Music]  [Music]  all right so if you were just listening  and you weren't watching along there  she's just dancing and making some cool  poses and having some fun with her  friends there's really nothing out of  the ordinary about it but despite all  this she had to give a response to  reporters marin has said in response to  the videos that she's agreed to take a  drug test which i don't think that she  should have had to do or should have  been pressured into but the results of  that drug test are supposedly going to  come out within the week and she's also  made the statement i did nothing illegal  which is very much true and even in my  teenage years i have not used any kind  of drug and then in response to the idea  of like oh well what if an emergency  came up uh she said i don't remember a  single time that there was a sudden  situation in the middle of the night to  go to the state council palace i think  my ability to function was really good  there were no known meetings on the days  i was partying so this readiness to  respond if there was an attack or  something seems to be based on the  presumption that she was drinking and we  don't know by the way if she was  drinking or drinking to excess but even  if she was like this is not a standard  that we hold to other leaders other  world leaders that they can't have a  drink every now and then that they can't  get a little buzz going why is this  being unfairly applied to her and then  after the initial clips came out we also  got a clip of marin dancing with someone  who is not her husband and some people  were upset with that even though if you  look at the video the dancing seems  pretty platonic and she's actually  trying to back away from the guy who's  making advances on her she at one point  puts her arm up so that's the situation  anyway for her to deal with her husband  with right it's not really a matter of  public interest in my opinion but just  it's another thing that they can  criticize her for and the big takeaway  really is that people need to chill out  a little bit and let loose and not take  things so seriously all the time and if  you're one of those people who are just  too uptight and you can't let loose  every now and then at least let other  people let loose and not take things so  seriously all the time and also let's  apply these criticisms equally please  like when donald trump danced to the  ymca  people were making criticisms about his  dancing abilities right because it  looked kind of awkward but aside from  that no one was saying oh he needs to  take a drug test and this is unbecoming  of a president of the united states and  what if we were attacked at that given  moment would he have been able to  respond no one was saying that but  apparently people are willing to make  these criticisms against marin because  she actually can dance and she's young  and a woman and all these different  things so it's definitely a double  standard it's pretty transparent and the  bottom line is people just need to chill  out and apply these standards equally so  we have a bit of a light-hearted story  to wrap things up today and it has to do  with one of the worst pandemic inspired  changes to our society which is of  course the dreaded qr code at  restaurants replacing physical menus we  know that during the pandemic businesses  would try to take advantage of the  situation by not providing us with  things that we were used to and just  using kobat as an excuse like they would  say oh sorry we can't clean your hotel  room because of covid and sorry you  can't bring your reusable bag to the  grocery store because of coba remember  that one well none of these changes were  as bad as the dreaded qr code scanner at  restaurants and while some of the  pandemic era inconveniences are no more  the dreaded qr code at restaurants  persist and the idea of introducing them  in the first place was pretty clear you  don't have people touching the menus  that way you don't have to sanitize the  menus as often and it's the same reason  why restaurants during the height of the  pandemic got rid of the ketchup bottles  on the tables and the salt and pepper  shakers and it didn't take long for us  to learn that the virus was largely an  airborne transmitted virus it didn't  really transfer that much from surfaces  so a lot of these changes that we made  were pointless and we could have  backtracked on them right then and there  pretty early on in the pandemic but  restaurants persisted with the qr thing  because printing menus can be expensive  you need to replace them sometimes when  they get dirty or when you change the  menu you got to think about the printing  costs and it's also in a low labor  environment just better for businesses  to have the qr codes because you don't  have to have staff distribute and  collect the menus but customers  absolutely revile the qr code myself  included a recent technomics survey  found that about 88 percent of  respondents said that they preferred  paper menus to digital qr codes about 66  percent of respondents agreed or  strongly agreed that they didn't like qr  codes because they involved pulling out  your phone as soon as you sit down at  the table about 57 agreed that using qr  codes felt like a chore and 55 agreed  that qr codes were hard to read and  browse through and it actually does seem  to make sense for restaurants to bring  back the physical menus now not just  because customers hate it and they'll  sometimes leave these awful reviews for  restaurants because of the qr codes the  qr codes actually are leading to people  ordering less because if you have a menu  left on the table for example sometimes  it'll have the pictures of the food and  the drinks and the desserts and  everything so you may be tempted to  order more just by giving a glance over  at it and saying oh that looks good i  want to order that whereas if you have  to pull out your phone scan the qr code  open up the website scroll down find  what you're looking for that's more of  an active action versus a passive action  of just glancing at something and saying  that looks good i want that now  depending on my mood i will sometimes  lie at the restaurant and i'll say i  don't have a phone or i have a flip  phone and so i need a physical menu that  is something that you can try out at  home there they'll have a few physical  menus at their ready so they're probably  not going to be happy to give it to you  but you can always just make up an  excuse and i'm sure you'll get it and  another pro tip for dealing with the  other inconvenience that people  absolutely hate at restaurants is when  you're about to pay for the meal just  have cash handy with the tip included so  that when the server comes over you can  just pay for it all at once they bring  you the check you look at the amount you  probably know about what it's going to  be you just give them the cash they go  on with it rather than having to give  them a card they leave come back and  then you fill out the tip and everything  it saves you about half the headache  because that's one of the things that  people hate most about restaurants  having to wait at the end of your meal  when you just want to get up and leave  all right that's going to do it for  today's show my thank you to david for  allowing me to fill in for him today  while he is traveling up in montreal and  we're going to have farron cousins fill  in the next couple of days david will be  back on thursday and friday to finish  out the week  and if you want more of the david pakman  show be sure to check out today's bonus  show which you can access by signing up  for a membership at joinpacman.com  or contributing to patreon at the five  dollar level at patreon.com  davidpakinshow i'll see yo